Guest: Well, most American food actually comes from other cultures and is then mixed into something new.
Host: Can you give us an example?
Guest: Take nachos. They are just corn chips covered in cheese, first made by a cook for some hungry visitors.
Host: And what about gumbo?
Guest: Gumbo is a spicy stew invented in New Orleans. It mixes several cooking styles in one pot.
Host: So American food is really a mix of the whole world.
Guest: Exactly. That spirit of mixing is what makes it special.', '主持人问美国是否有自己的食物;嘉宾说大多源自别的文化,再融合出新东西;以墨西哥玉米片为例,是裹奶酪的玉米片,由厨师为饥饿的客人首创;秋葵汤是新奥尔良发明的辣味炖菜,一锅融合多种烹饪;主持人总结美式食物是全世界的融合,嘉宾说正是这种融合精神让它特别。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the guest say about most American food?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It comes from other cultures and is mixed into something new.","It was all invented in America alone.","It never changes over time.","It comes only from France."]},{"q":"What are nachos, according to the guest?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A sweet cake.","Corn chips covered in cheese.","A bowl of rice.","A cold drink."]},{"q":"Where was gumbo invented?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In New Orleans.","In China.","In Mexico.","In nobody''s kitchen."]},{"q":"How is gumbo described?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A cold sweet soup.","A spicy stew that mixes several styles.","A simple drink.","A plain bread."]},{"q":"What makes American food special, the guest says?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Its very high price.","Its single origin.","Its spirit of mixing cultures.","Its lack of taste."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3');
It is likely that they moved there many thousands of years ago.
After the arrival of the Europeans, the native people suffered greatly.
Many died from new diseases, while others were forced to leave their land.
Even so, some survived, and their culture is still part of the state today.', '没人确切知道最早的人何时到达今天的加利福尼亚;很可能是数千年前迁来的;欧洲人到来后,原住民遭受了巨大苦难;许多人死于新的疾病,另一些被迫离开家园;尽管如此,仍有人幸存下来,他们的文化至今仍是这个州的一部分。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is unknown about the first people of California?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Whether they ate fish.","What colour their houses were.","How tall they were.","The exact time when they arrived."]},{"q":"When did they probably move there?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Many thousands of years ago.","Last year.","A few months ago.","Only after the Europeans came."]},{"q":"What happened after the Europeans arrived?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Everyone became rich.","The native people suffered greatly.","Nothing changed.","The Europeans left at once."]},{"q":"Why did many native people die?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Because of the cold weather only.","Because they refused to eat.","Because of new diseases.","Because they moved to Europe."]},{"q":"What does the passage say about their culture today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It has completely disappeared.","It was never important.","It moved to another country.","It is still part of the state."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3');
Tom: I''d love to. I''ve never been there before.
Mia: Great. We can enter through the old Dragon Gate first.
Tom: Was it really built with materials from China?
Mia: Yes, the materials were donated from China many years ago.
Tom: Amazing. Can we taste some traditional food too?
Mia: Of course. There''s food to suit every taste, and the tea shops are wonderful.
Tom: Then let''s go. I can''t wait!', '米娅问汤姆下午是否有空,想带他逛唐人街;汤姆乐意,说从没去过;米娅说先从龙门进去;汤姆问龙门是否真是用中国的材料建的;米娅说材料多年前由中国捐赠;汤姆想尝尝传统食物;米娅说有适合各种口味的食物,茶馆也很棒;汤姆迫不及待要去。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Mia offer to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Show Tom around Chinatown.","Cook dinner at home.","Take a train to Mexico.","Sell Tom a hotel."]},{"q":"Has Tom been to Chinatown before?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Yes, many times.","No, never before.","Only last week.","He lives there."]},{"q":"How was the Dragon Gate built?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["With cheap plastic.","By the visitors themselves.","With materials donated from China.","With no materials at all."]},{"q":"What does Mia say about the food there?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It is always too spicy.","There is none left.","It is only for tourists.","There is food to suit every taste."]},{"q":"How does Tom feel at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He can''t wait to go.","He is too tired to go.","He no longer wants to go.","He has changed his mind."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3');
This instrument has a history of more than a thousand years.
It is even mentioned in the oldest collection of Chinese poetry.
At festivals, villagers play it while others dance in their best clothing.
Listening to it, visitors feel they have stepped into a different and beautiful world.', '在许多少数民族村寨,人们仍演奏一种叫芦笙的古老乐器;它有一千多年的历史;甚至在最古老的中国诗歌总集中也被提到;节日里,村民演奏它,其他人则穿着最好的服装起舞;听着它,游客觉得仿佛走进了一个不同而美丽的世界。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where do people still play the lusheng?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["In big office buildings.","In ethnic minority villages.","On the ocean.","In foreign countries only."]},{"q":"How old is this instrument?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only a few years old.","About one hundred years.","More than a thousand years.","Nobody plays it now."]},{"q":"Where is the instrument mentioned?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["In a modern comic book.","On a food menu.","In a science report.","In the oldest collection of Chinese poetry."]},{"q":"What do villagers do at festivals?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Play it while others dance in fine clothing.","Sell it to tourists.","Hide it away.","Break it on purpose."]},{"q":"How do visitors feel when they listen?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Bored and tired.","As if they had entered a different, beautiful world.","Angry and afraid.","Hungry for food."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3');
Ben: I''m thinking of a spicy stew from my hometown.
Ann: Spicy? I''m not sure I can eat very hot food.
Ben: Don''t worry, I''ll make a mild one for you.
Ann: Thank you. I''ll bring some dumplings, then.
Ben: Perfect. So the table will have food from two cultures.
Ann: Exactly. That''s the best part of sharing a meal.
Ben: I agree. See you on Saturday!', '安说周末有聚餐,问本带什么菜;本想带家乡的辣味炖菜;安说自己吃不了太辣;本说会给她做一份温和不辣的;安道谢,说那她带饺子;本说桌上就有来自两种文化的食物了;安说这正是分享一餐最棒的地方;两人约好周六见。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What event are Ann and Ben talking about?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A football match.","A long camping trip.","A potluck dinner this weekend.","A music exam."]},{"q":"What dish does Ben plan to bring?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["A sweet cake.","A cold salad.","A bowl of plain rice.","A spicy stew from his hometown."]},{"q":"Why is Ann unsure about the dish?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She may not be able to eat very hot food.","It costs too much.","It is too far away.","It takes too long to cook."]},{"q":"What does Ben say he will do for Ann?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Cancel the dinner.","Make a mild one for her.","Buy her a gift.","Bring no food at all."]},{"q":"What does Ann like best about sharing a meal?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Eating alone.","Saving money.","Having food from two cultures on the table.","Cooking nothing herself."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required3', 'U3');
Walk down one street and you may hear many different languages being spoken.
People of different backgrounds live side by side, sharing the same shops and streets.
Some worry that life there is hard, but many residents feel quite at home.
For them, the rich mix of cultures is a gift to be treasured, not a problem.', '有些社区非常多元,近一半的人出生在别的国家;走在一条街上,你可能听到许多种不同的语言;不同背景的人比邻而居,共享同样的商店和街道;有人担心那里生活艰难,但许多居民觉得很自在;对他们来说,丰富的文化融合是一份值得珍惜的礼物,而非难题。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How diverse are these neighbourhoods?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Everyone was born in the same town.","No one lives there.","Only one language is spoken.","Almost half the people were born in another country."]},{"q":"What might you hear walking down one street?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Many different languages.","Total silence.","Only one song.","Nothing but cars."]},{"q":"How do people of different backgrounds live?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Far apart from one another.","Side by side, sharing the same streets.","In separate countries.","Without any shops."]},{"q":"How do many residents feel about living there?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Lost and unwelcome.","Eager to leave at once.","Quite at home.","Sorry that they came."]},{"q":"How do they see the mix of cultures?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["As a serious problem.","As something useless.","As a reason to move away.","As a gift to be treasured."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required3', 'U3');

